# Protections for the path-traversal / arbitrary-file-read corpus (CWE-22). Held
# IDENTICAL -- byte-identical, not merely equivalent -- across every target in this
# family on purpose: the *flawed containment filter the escape has to defeat* is the
# only variable, so a protection difference would confound the measurement. The
# negative control shares this exact file too, which is what makes its refusal
# attributable to the absence of the bug rather than to different hardening.
#
# EVERY PROTECTION IS ON, AND NONE OF THEM MATTERS. That is the point of the
# category, not an oversight. This is a non-memory-corruption route: nothing
# overflows, no pointer is written, no code address is ever needed, and no byte of
# the program's memory is ever corrupted. The entire payload is a FILENAME typed
# into the target's own request protocol.
#
# -fstack-protector-all  a canary detects a corrupted return address in an
#                        epilogue. Nothing here writes past a buffer -- the one
#                        target that depends on a buffer LIMIT (trav_14) depends on
#                        snprintf() TRUNCATING, which is the bounded, defined
#                        behaviour, not on it overflowing. No frame is ever damaged
#                        and the check always passes.
# -pie -fPIE             PIE randomises where code and data live. No exploit step
#                        here needs any address at all; the "payload" is a path.
# -Wl,-z,relro,-z,now    Full RELRO write-protects the GOT after startup. There is
#                        no GOT write in this category and no pointer write of any
#                        kind. The program calls exactly the functions it was
#                        linked against, in the order it was written to call them.
#                        It simply calls open() on a name that resolves outside the
#                        directory the program believes it is confined to.
# (NX)                   comes from the default ELF program headers; nothing is
#                        ever executed from a data page, so it is satisfied too.
#
# Building the family with the full modern set keeps "hardened" from being quietly
# re-learned as "not exploitable" -- and here it is stronger than that: it shows
# that for this category the entire memory-safety mitigation stack is not merely
# insufficient, it is *irrelevant*, because none of it is in the exploit's path.
#
# -O0                    load-bearing for the MEASUREMENT, not for the bug. Two
#                        things depend on it. First, the family has to be a
#                        controlled comparison, and at higher -O gcc is free to
#                        reorganise each target's filter differently. Second, the
#                        executor derives WHERE operator text is concatenated into
#                        a path by matching the snprintf() destination and the
#                        open() argument to the same frame slot
#                        (`lea -0xNN(%rbp)`); at -O2 that buffer can live in a
#                        register and the derivation would have nothing to match,
#                        so the gate would be guessing where it is currently
#                        reading. The bug itself is a missing/flawed
#                        canonicalisation and is entirely unaffected by
#                        optimisation level.
-fstack-protector-all
-pie
-fPIE
-Wl,-z,relro,-z,now
-O0
